
## Chapter 5, Section B: Microeconomic Cost Breakdown per Patient Episode## ── Comparative Analysis of Direct Medical Costs in the Japanese and United States Healthcare Markets ──
To validate the macroeconomic structural reductions, this section provides a verified micro-costing matrix per individual patient per therapeutic episode. By stripping away monopoly premiums through an open-source framework and shifting to an outpatient infrastructure, the total expenditure per episode is reduced to approximately ¥3,200,000 in Japan and $30,000 in the United States.
------------------------------
## 1. Japanese Healthcare Market (National Health Insurance Framework)
Calculated based on current National Health Insurance (NHI) drug price standards and standard disposable medical device manufacturing logistics in Japan.

* I. Preemptive Niche Regulation & Adjunctive Pharmaceuticals: Approx. ¥120,000
* Generic G-CSF Formulations (e.g., Filgrastim injection): Approx. ¥30,000 (NHI standard)
   * Selective Immunosuppression (e.g., Oral Tacrolimus, 30-day supply): Approx. ¥40,000
   * Prophylactic Antivirals (Acyclovir) & Empiric Antimicrobials: Approx. ¥50,000
* II. Off-the-Shelf Allogeneic Stealth Cellular Payload (1 Unit Vial): Approx. ¥2,800,000
* Cost Architecture: Industrialized mass-scale bioreactor expansion & cryopreservation overhead (¥1,500,000) + Quality Control (QC) & logistics validation (¥500,000) + Non-profit consortium institutional maintenance baseline (¥800,000).
   * Note: This optimizes the economies of scale by eliminating the hyper-individuation manufacturing friction and commercial markups that dictate current ¥40,000,000 autologous CAR-T pricing.
* III. Specialized Infusion Disposables: Approx. ¥30,000
* Sterile Multi-Chamber Bedside Reconstitution Container: Approx. ¥10,000
   * Biocompatible Non-Adherent Fluidic Administration Set (MPC Polymer Coated): Approx. ¥20,000
* IV. Outpatient Infusion Suite Utilization & Technical Fees: Approx. ¥50,000
* Includes outpatient chair/bed assignment fees, nursing technical administration tariffs, and two localized 3T-MRI diagnostic imaging scans under standard Japanese fee schedules.

👉 【Total Direct Medical Cost (Pre-Insurance): Approx. ¥3,000,000 – ¥3,200,000】

* Socio-Economic Fact: Under Japan's universal coverage and the High-Cost Medical Expense Benefit System (Kogaku-Ryohohi-Seido), the actual out-of-pocket liability for the individual patient at the clinical counter is capped at ¥20,000 to ¥100,000 (dependent upon income brackets), ensuring absolute universal access.

