## 2. United States Healthcare Market (Commercial & Public Payer Framework)
Calculated using U.S. generic drug procurement conventions, standard outpatient ambulatory facility fees, and industrialized biologic tier pricing.

* I. Mobilization & Immunosuppression (Generic Small Molecules/Peptides): $1,500
* Standard tier pricing for generic G-CSF, oral Tacrolimus, and prophylactic Acyclovir regimens.
* II. Industrialized Off-the-Shelf Allogeneic Stealth Cell Payload: $20,000
* Stabilized near-cost bulk manufacturing pricing under open-source patent pool governance.
* III. Specialized Disposables (Frangible Reconstitution Bag & MPC Line): $500
* IV. Outpatient Ambulatory Infusion Suite & 3T-MRI Technical/Professional Fees: $8,000
* Note: Reflecting U.S. healthcare delivery paradigms, facility fees and professional radiological interpretation tariffs for two 3T-MRI scans are adjusted higher to match realistic commercial insurance reimbursement benchmarks.

👉 【Total Direct Medical Cost (Payer Billing Base): $30,000 (Approx. ¥4.5 Million)】

* Socio-Economic Fact: This represents a 95% to 97% vertical contraction compared to the contemporary U.S. total episode cost ($600,000–$1,000,000) for autologous CAR-T or myeloablative HSCT. It systematically mitigates private insurer insolvency risks and eliminates patient-level medical bankruptcy.

